cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on the experiments, please cite both the software release and the paper below."
title: "The Price of Compliance: emission-mask-constrained adversarial attacks on deep learning spectrum sensing in the 5.9 GHz ITS band (research framework)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dhankhar"
    given-names: "Parveen"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Vaish College of Engineering, Rohtak, India"
  - family-names: "Vats"
    given-names: "Davesh"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Vaish College of Engineering, Rohtak, India"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Daveshvats/v2x_adversarial_sensing"
abstract: >-
  Phase-1 research framework: the compliance-constrained ("Compliant
  Attacker") threat model for deep learning spectrum sensing in the
  post-FCC 5.9 GHz ITS band. Contains: post-coexistence waveform
  generators (C-V2X PC5, 802.11p, U-NII-4 WiFi, plus real over-the-air
  802.11 captures, CC BY-NC-SA), TR 37.885-inspired channels, a
  differentiable receiver front-end, the mask-constrained waveform-domain
  PGD attack, mask-matched adversarial training and TRADES defenses, a
  second victim architecture with surrogate transfer, a 3-training-seed
  protocol, MEAP / Price-of-Compliance physical robustness metrics, a
  power-amplifier (Rapp) regrowth reality check with PA-aware
  re-optimization, and the one-command v2x-redteam evaluation CLI. All
  result JSONs embed configuration and seeds; every paper claim is traced
  to a result JSON (paper/CLAIMS.md). Code: MIT; embedded real-capture
  data: CC BY-NC-SA. Runs on CPU only.
keywords:
  - "spectrum sensing"
  - "V2X"
  - "C-V2X"
  - "adversarial machine learning"
  - "emission mask"
  - "wireless security"
  - "deep learning"
